2186045417] [17592186338373 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186337480 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338373 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186337731 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338373 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186337982 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338373 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338373 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338373 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186337480 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338373 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "32bcf106-ea5d-53fa-a139-89e099b59c67" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338877 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186338373 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338877 #edb/ref 1069 "q-71029" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338877 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338877 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the straight line with the vector equation\n\n$$\nr=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nfor $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$ Find the Cartesian equation of this line." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186338877 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "db08ec21-5e10-5fa9-a587-34ff723a0e65" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186338877 #edb/ref 1074 "We have the vector equation \n\n$$\nr=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}+t\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix},\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nThis implies that the straight line passes through the point $P(3,4,-5)$ and is parallel to the vector $v=⟨4,6,9⟩.$ So, its Cartesian (canonical) equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-3}{4}=\\frac{y-4}{6}=\\frac{z-(-5)}{9}=t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\n$$\n\nSimplifying, we reach\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-3}{4}=\\frac{y-4}{6}=\\frac{z+5}{9}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186367227 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186367228 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367227 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186367229 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367227 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186367230 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367227 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186367231 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367227 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186367232 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367227 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367227 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367227 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186367228 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367227 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "4010e133-bb74-590a-aaad-0744ebb64de5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367228 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{x-2}{-5}=\\frac{y+3}{2}=\\frac{z-7}{-1}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367228 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367228 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "d9e78327-b43d-5969-8d3b-bed4609b49e0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367229 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{x-2}{-1}=\\frac{y+3}{2}=\\frac{z-7}{-5}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367229 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367229 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "415707ec-16c3-52eb-ae48-60f27d55babf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367230 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{x+5}{2}=\\frac{y-2}{-3}=\\frac{z+1}{7}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367230 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367230 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "ace39f4a-2512-5b36-8884-7fa037704cfc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367231 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{x+2}{-5}=\\frac{y+3}{2}=\\frac{z+7}{1}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367231 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367231 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e8680259-b972-51c1-a413-a39306c9e5d0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367232 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{x+5}{3}=\\frac{y-2}{-2}=\\frac{z+1}{7}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367232 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367232 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e0439e86-3ea3-5b81-8a8b-d0a949ba059f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367240 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186367241 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367240 #edb/ref 1069 "q-127534" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367240 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367240 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/f6/f65a9806a2d6736a9eed283253225f6e5405d3e272f25e9c6a763651a19d0a31.png)\n\nFind a Cartesian equation of the line shown in the figure above." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367240 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "26ccf3a9-18a6-5810-b58b-63343e2dbccc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367240 #edb/ref 1074 "We know that the line passes through the points $P(-1,2,5)$ and $Q(2,2,9).$ Now, we need to find a vector parallel to the given line. Let's consider the vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$ which is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PQ} & =⟨2,2,9⟩-⟨-1,2,5⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,0,4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the point $P$ and the vector $\\overset{\\to }{PQ}$, we have that the Cartesian (canonical) equation of the given line is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{x-(-1)}{3}=\\frac{y-2}{0}=\\frac{z-5}{4}=t,\\,t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),\n$$\n\nor equivalently\n\n$$\n\\frac{x+1}{3}=\\frac{y-2}{0}=\\frac{z-5}{4}.\n$$\n\nBut the above equation is problematic because $\\frac{y-2}{0}$ involves division by zero.\n\nHowever, in our line, the $y$ component always maintains the constant value of $y=2.$ For example, our two points $P(-1,2,5)$ and $Q(2,2,9)$ both have $y$-coordinates of $y=2.$\n\nSo, in the Cartesian equation, we remove the $\\frac{y-2}{0}$ part and instead write $y=2,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{x+1}{3}=\\frac{z-5}{4},\\,y=2\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367241 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186367242 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367241 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186367243 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367241 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186367244 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367241 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186367245 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367241 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186367246 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186367241 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [175921